course: dictionary
lesson: 8114
title: Rep: one short word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Rep» is a short word with more than one meaning. You cannot know which one is meant until you read the words around it. Those words are the context, and they are your best clue.
explain: «A class rep speaks for the class at the school council.» Here a rep is a person chosen to speak for a group. Ask yourself: what would fit? A person who speaks for others fits, so rep means representative.
explain: «Three sets of 10 reps» in PE is a different meaning. Here a rep is one repetition, one time doing a movement. The words sets and PE show you which meaning to choose.
fact: Rep is short for representative: a person chosen to speak or act for a group, like a class rep.
fact: A sales rep is a salesperson who visits customers for a company.
fact: In exercise, a rep means one repetition, doing a movement once: ten reps of sit-ups.
fact: Rep can also be slang for reputation, as in «he has a rep for being funny», or short for repertory theatre.
fact: Always check the clues around the word, then put your meaning into the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «A class rep speaks for the class at the school council.» What is a class rep? | A shop worker who sells things | A type of sit-up done in PE | A word for the whole school | *A person chosen to speak for the class
exercise: «Three sets of 10 reps» in PE means what? | Ten sales visits in one day | *Ten times doing one movement, in each of three sets | Ten pupils in one team | Ten classes in three rooms
exercise: «He has a rep for being funny.» What does rep mean here? | A person chosen to speak for others | *Reputation: what people generally think of him | One time doing a movement | A set of tools for cooking
test: «The council has a budget, a fixed amount of money, so it must choose; a good rep listens to the teachers' reasons too.» What does a good rep do? | *Listens to others and carries messages both ways | Only talks about sport | Ignores the teachers | Keeps the money for himself
test: A friend says, «My sales rep is coming on Monday.» What is a sales rep? | A pupil who represents the class | A repeat of a movement | *A salesperson who visits customers for a company | An actor in a theatre
exam: «Think of deciding on a class trip: a few class reps can choose.» What does rep mean in this sentence? | One set of exercises | Reputation, what people think of you | *People chosen to speak for their class | A trip to a theatre
